(* Variant mimic-key: the mimic path, as the code has it, against an attacker that holds the REALITY private key of the
   server (AUD-7, #425): the key that the public key of the link pins. This is the middlebox in the best position that it
   can have on this path: it opens every proof, answers alice with a temporary certificate of its own, so that her sidecar
   hands her node the stream, and opens a REALITY session of its own to the server with her short id. The binding of the
   Noise handshake to the exporter of each session is what must stop it, as on TLS-443 (tls443-cert). *)

(* The attacker that holds the REALITY key makes the key share of every ClientHello that it sends, so the prover would
   select attacker(tpk(a)) in the hypothesis of a rule whose conclusion matches it, and run without end: it did not
   finish in 900 s. The prover suggests this declaration, which changes only the order in which it resolves the rules,
   not what it proves; with it the variant answers in about a minute. *)
noselect a: bitstring; attacker(tpk(a)).

process
  ( Setup()
  | MimicSetup()
  | LeakRealityKey()
  | MimicSessions(bt_export, kp_on)
  )
